ext{new}, y_p)$ is $y'_p = -1.$\n\nNow, we compute $\\Delta y$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(5\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot (-1)-(-1))\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed row is as given below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,x\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,y\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,y'\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta y_p$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y_p$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y'_p$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta y$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-\\dfrac74$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid gainsboro]{-\\dfrac{1}{4}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" 13194139540373 17592186576411 true] [17592186221164 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c,\n$$\n\nthe $2$-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton (ABM2) metho