 component-wise.\n\nFirst, because the initial conditions are $y(0)=1$ and $z(0)=-2,$ we place $y=1$ and $z=-2$ in the table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$\\Delta y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nNext, we compute both $y'$ and $z'$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=-2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =-4xz+3y+2x \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0+3+0 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$\\Delta y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFinally, we compute $\\Delta y$ and $\\Delta z$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$\\Delta y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $\\Delta x$ to $x,$ $\\Delta y$ to $y,$ and $\\Delta z$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+(-2)=-1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-2+3=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$\\Delta y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z'$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\Delta z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"solid\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1) \\approx -1.\n$$" 13194139540373 17592186576411 true] [17592186221173 1074 "For a second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' = f(x,y,y'), \\qquad y(a) = c, \\quad y'(a) = d,\n$$\n\nwe can use Euler's method to approximate a solution by first reducing the s