is to expand this table by using the **smoothness property**. In the next slide, we will apply this property to derive a new transform without computing integrals from scratch." 13194139540373 17592186576411 false] [17592186222517 1064 "Using the smoothness property, we can now add transforms involving factors of $t$ and higher powers of $t$ by differentiating previously known formulas.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(t)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$F(s)=\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\}$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Domain</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t e^{kt}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{(s-k)^2}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s>k$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t^2 e^{kt}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{2}{(s-k)^3}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s>k$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t\\sin \\omega t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{2\\omega s}{(s^2+\\omega^2)^2}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s>0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t^2\\sin \\omega t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{2\\omega(3s^2-\\omega^2)}{(s^2+\\omega^2)^3}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s>0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t\\cos \\omega t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{s^2-\\omega^2}{(s^2+\\omega^2)^2}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s>0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t^2\\cos \\omega t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{2s(s^2-3\\omega^2)}{(s^2+\\omega^