$ | $0$ |\n| $-2$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ |\n\n**III.**\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-5$ | $-1$ |\n| $-2$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ |\n\n**IV.**\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-5$ | $0$ |\n| $-2$ | $0$ |\n| $8$ | $0$ |" 13194139540373 17592186576411 false] [17592186225083 1074 "We are given the function\n\n$$\ns(x) = (x - 8)(x + 2)(x + 5)\n$$\n\nand asked to evaluate the transformed expression\n\n$$\ny = s(x) + 1\n$$\n\nfor different values of $x$.\n\nFirst, we note that $s(x)$ has roots at $x=-5, x=-2$, and $x=8$. Therefore, a table of values for $s(x)$ at these points is as follows:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$s(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\ny = s(x) + 1\n$$\n\nthe correct table for $y$ must be the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" 13194139540373 17592186576411 true] [17592186225083 1074 "We are given the function\n\n$$\ns(x) = (x - 8)(x + 2)(x + 5)\n$$\n\nand asked to evaluate the transformed expression\n\n$$\ny = s(x) + 1\n$$\n\nfor different values of $x$.\n\nFirst, we note that $s(x)$ has roots at $x=-5, x=-2$, and $x=8$. Therefore, a table of values for $s(x)$ at these points is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $s(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-5$ | $0$ |\n| $-2$ | $0$ |\n| $8$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\ny = s(x) + 1\n$$\n\nthe correct table for $y$ must be the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-5$ | $1$ |\n| $-2$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ |" 13194139540373 17592186576411 false] [17592186225084 1074 "We are given the exponential function\n\n$$\np(x) = 24 \\cdot 3^x\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $p(x)$ at three different $x$-values.\n\n- When $x = -1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(-1) &= 24 \\cdot 3^{-1} \\\\\n&= 24 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $x = 0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(0) &= 24 \\cdot 3^{0} \\\\\n&= 24 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $x = 1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(1) &= 24 \\cdot 3^{1} \\\\\n&= 24 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 72\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the table that matches the function is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$p(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$72$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" 13194139540373 17592186576411 true] [17592186225084 1074 "We are give